{"availability":"available","full":"illm4tic/wolf-world","name":"wolf-world","description":"Interactive third-person Three.js demo where you control an animated wolf, explore a 3D scene, and switch between walk, run, creep, sit, camera follow, zoom, and collision interactions.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-19T07:51:55Z","updated":"2026-05-19T08:29:05Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://wolf.yeezus.cn/","topics":["3d","third-person-camera","threejs","webgl","wolf"],"demo":"https://wolf.yeezus.cn/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:41:17.894Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:41:17.894Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:41:17.894Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:41:17.894Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive third-person 3D demo centered around a wolf character.","Wolf World invites users into a small 3D environment where they can explore the scene, control an animated wolf, and experience movement, running, creeping, sitting, and camera-follow interactions. The project is designed to feel lightweight and approachable, making it a good fit for character showcases, scene previews, and simple interactive demos.","The core idea of the project is simple: enter the scene and explore it through a character-driven experience. Users first land on an entry page, then move into the 3D demo area. The wolf transitions between actions based on player input, while the third-person camera helps create a more immersive viewing experience."],"features":["Wolf-centered presentation with animated character interaction","Smooth switching between idle, walk, run, creep, and sit states","Third-person camera follow and zoom interaction","Separate landing page and demo page for showcase-style presentation","Lightweight structure that can be extended into a richer character demo or scene prototype"],"sourceUrl":"https://git